# Definition of Done

ABADAR should **not** be considered finished because:

```text
the UI looks good
```

or:

```text
orders can be submitted
```

The project is finished when you can demonstrate:

## Correctness

```text
✓ Matching rules are correct
✓ Balances are conserved
✓ Orders cannot execute beyond limits
✓ Duplicate events do not duplicate state
```

## Concurrency

```text
✓ Concurrent orders are safe
✓ Race detector passes
✓ Order sequencing is deterministic
```

## Distributed Systems

```text
✓ Events are durable
✓ Consumers recover
✓ Events can be replayed
✓ Services can scale horizontally
```

## Reliability

```text
✓ Service crashes are recoverable
✓ Kafka failures are handled
✓ Database failures are handled
✓ Matching state can be restored
```

## Observability

```text
✓ Metrics exist
✓ Logs are structured
✓ Distributed traces exist
✓ Kafka lag is visible
```

## Performance

```text
✓ Load tests exist
✓ Benchmarks exist
✓ Bottlenecks have been identified
✓ Optimizations are measured
```

